 "timeout_semantic_change": {
  "before": "7c7f7dd: every probe timeout — including a subject that was dispatched and did not finish — was UNRUNNABLE / ENVIRONMENT, no verdict (RFC §9 listed timeout among harness failures; recorded as a residual in the original P2-PROBE-PROTOCOL.json)",
  "after": {
   "harness cannot launch / tool unavailable / sandbox unavailable / probe or watchdog fails or times out before an observation": "UNRUNNABLE; ENVIRONMENT; no BehaviorVerdict",
   "subject dispatched, the spec's observation window expires": "EXECUTED; the verdict the spec's observable assigns to an expired window",
   "spec whose observable cannot assign semantics to its bounded window": "INVALID_SPEC; rejected at StaticPlanAdmission (check 9) and by the probe"
  },
  "no_global_rule": "neither 'subject timeout -> REFUTED' nor 'subject timeout -> UNRUNNABLE'; the verdict of an expired window is the observation class's (python_callable): {\"exists\": \"REFUTED\", \"returns\": \"REFUTED\", \"raises\": \"REFUTED\", \"blocks\": \"SATISFIED\"}",
  "implementation": "RFC §9.2 (V2-002). The harness watchdog (ExecutionEnv.timeout_s) runs until the harness reports DISPATCHED: its expiry, a launch failure or a lost protocol is HARNESS_FAILED -> UNRUNNABLE / ENVIRONMENT (TIME-1). From DISPATCHED the spec's own window runs (observable.within_s: required, positive, finite); its expiry is SUBJECT_DEADLINE -> EXECUTED with the verdict the observation class assigns to a window in which nothing arrived: exists / returns / raises -> REFUTED (the awaited fact did not occur), blocks -> SATISFIED (the call was still running). A spec with no bounded window is INVALID_SPEC before anything runs",
  "evidence": {
   "subject_deadline": {
    "returns 3, MUST_HOLD": {
     "status": "EXECUTED",
     "behavior_verdict": "REFUTED",
